// REJECTED — G1: the stream a `subscribe` names is an ordinary head and must
// resolve. `nostream` is neither a local, a required key, nor a callable.
//
// This fixture is the SAFE-DIRECTION half of a divergence that hid an unsafe
// one. `subscribe` is a keyword, so the self-hosted gate's expression grammar
// stopped dead on it: the whole `let` run became a skip. A skipped run binds no
// handle, which falsely refused five documents of this repo's corpus — and a
// skipped run resolves no heads either, so THIS program raised no objection at
// all while the reference refused it (item 130 Slice 1).
//
// The handle is deliberately never read back after the bracket: a later
// `sub.next()` would have drawn the gate's OWN wrong refusal (`sub` undeclared)
// and hidden the silence behind a message mismatch. Nothing here names `sub`
// twice, so the only verdict on offer is the one about `nostream`.
//
// expected error:
//   `nostream` is not a declared requirement of Orders

component Orders {
  let sub = subscribe nostream undo sub.close()
}
